    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you, but that feels like just a bandaid. i've been thinking about it from a different angle though... like, if we look at it objectively, if nothing has any inherent meaning, then the value of staying alive vs. not staying alive is basically zero. it's just a net neutral. if it's all mathematically equal, why is there such a massive bias toward choosing to stay?",
